    "implementation_delta": "Publish AccelerateObjectiveIdentityParity@1 as the Accelerate-owned hermetic proof that the PCPR-080 Python client and the PCPR-081 generic MCP client submit the same canonical PCPR-060 objective bytes to the same canonical service and receive the same objective identity and equivalent goals, tasks, events, candidate evidence, and final receipts. Python client CID baguqeerat346yf4k7kenbqlbtyejeilgxamna262z3axzjjatzm2hccehblq and MCP client CID baguqeerasdkirdryda7uoi5gchsyhuyvh6d2uremm45zpob7hoss3ao66ahq remain distinct and are not reminted. Objective CID baguqeeraynsn7tjr3iaggnreylzxo3akaooqwp5bf5oheaa6eubth2zwqeba, idea digest baguqeeracbayojdov4jmqiirx22pavrg6nabazcocru6y3scrdx5e54mw2zq, pack CID bafkreih72d3nncekez43wmtlczq5mdtymzniluujypwybpgu3mtt7i4v2e, current-root CID bafkreihjdjarrlr24sperlq3zl4hjrksbol4b5saxquie3wpyi6xwsobwi, and chain CID baguqeeraeuvfodvledfa4nvfuso6eyyytzk2acptcogzwzyarkdinpqcsdfq are bound and not reminted. Replaying the same parity command yields parity CID baguqeera6y3w7bhzy6hpo6ohfsrj5xihrw5vk6qqljjonjrupijd2yrp3hnq and is rejected as a duplicate effect. Both client principals remain intent, never authority. DatasetsObjectiveIdentityParityBinding@1 and KitObjectiveIdentityParityBinding@1 consume the Accelerate parity proof without reminting pack, current-root, chain, objective, protocol, Python-client, or MCP-client identities. Live Supervisor.run, live Quack, live MCP stdio/HTTP, and live CLI stay typed unavailable. Missing a live Quack-fenced session emits operator-blocking task pcpr-082-operator-live-cross-client-objective-identity-parity. Authority-bypass proof remains PCPR-083. This evaluator never writes DuckDB or Quack state and never emits a closed PCPR release outcome."
  },
